  "cues": [
   [
    0.104,
    "Remember the activation energy barrier from last lesson, the hump a reaction must climb."
   ],
   [
    5.664,
    "The active site can lower that hump in four ways."
   ],
   [
    8.659,
    "First, it orients the substrates correctly, so they meet in just the right position."
   ],
   [
    14.141,
    "Second, it strains the substrate's bonds, stretching them so they break more easily."
   ],
   [
    19.688,
    "Third, it provides a favourable microenvironment."
   ],
   [
    23.164,
    "For example, the pocket can be more acidic than the cell around it."
   ],
   [
    27.357,
    "Fourth, it can bond covalently to the substrate for a moment, and then let go."
   ],
   [
    32.253,
    "Whichever way it works, the hump gets lower, and the reaction speeds up."
   ],
   [
    36.758,
    "But the energy change, delta G, stays exactly the same."
   ]
  ]
 },
